      "Performs well on smooth, honed, and glossy paver finishes where haze is normally hardest to avoid",
      "Eight standard color options cover the most common paver tones",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Gel-based chemistry sets quickly, leaving less margin for error on large jobs tackled solo",
      "Narrower effective joint range (1/8 to 1.5 inches) than some wide-joint-rated competitors",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The no-haze specialist. If you're installing on smooth or dark pavers where haze shows up starkly, HP NextGel is the safest bet in the category.",
    description:
      "Techniseal built its reputation on haze-resistant technology, and HP NextGel is the clearest expression of that focus. Standard polymeric sands rely on a binder that partially dissolves and travels with the misting water; some of that binder inevitably ends up drying as a chalky white film on the paver face. Techniseal's NextGel binder is formulated differently — it's designed to gel and lock into the sand matrix almost immediately upon contact with water, rather than staying in solution long enough to migrate onto the surrounding pavers. In our side-by-side haze test on honed granite-look concrete pavers — a finish notoriously prone to haze because it has almost no surface texture to hide residue in — HP NextGel left a barely perceptible film that rinsed away completely with a garden hose, while two competing sands required scrubbing with a haze-removal solution. The tradeoff for that fast-gelling chemistry is a shorter forgiveness window: because the polymer begins locking in almost as soon as it's misted, you need to have your joints swept, compacted, and pre-wetted correctly before you start, since there's less opportunity to correct mistakes mid-application. HP NextGel cures to a firm, crack-resistant joint that held up through our freeze-thaw cycling test without visible fracturing. Coverage runs about 90 square feet per 50-lb bag on standard 1/4-inch joints, priced around $35-40 per bag. For anyone who has been burned by haze on a previous polymeric sand installation — especially on smooth or dark pavers where haze shows up starkly — HP NextGel is the safest bet in the category.",
  },
  {
    id: "dominator-1-jointing-sand",
    name: "DOMINATOR #1 Polymeric Jointing Sand",
    category: "Heavy-Duty Polymeric Sand",
    badge: "Best for Wide Joints",
