    cons: [
      "Coarser grain structure makes it difficult to sweep into joints narrower than 1/8 inch",
      "Longer full-cure time (up to 48 hours) than finer-grained competitors given the extra material volume in wide joints",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The only sand in this list we'd trust in a 2-inch flagstone joint. DOMINATOR #1 holds its shape and strength where finer formulas shrink and crack.",
    description:
      "Wide joints are where most polymeric sands fail — the same binder ratio that works perfectly in a quarter-inch paver joint often can't provide enough structural integrity to fill and hold a 2-inch flagstone gap without shrinking or crumbling as it dries. DOMINATOR #1 is formulated specifically to solve that problem, with a higher polymer-to-sand ratio and a coarser aggregate blend designed to build strength through the full depth of an oversized joint. In our flagstone test bed, we filled joints ranging from 1 inch to just over 2.5 inches and found DOMINATOR held its shape and volume through curing far better than the standard-formula sands we tried in the same joints, several of which visibly shrank and cracked at the surface within a week. That structural bulk comes with tradeoffs. The grain size is noticeably coarser than most fine-joint polymeric sands, which makes it genuinely difficult to sweep into anything narrower than about 1/8 inch — it tends to bridge over tight joints rather than settling in. Full cure in deep joints also takes longer, up to 48 hours in cool weather, because there's simply more material that needs to set up throughout its depth; rushing this with early foot traffic can leave a soft, dented surface. Haze risk is moderate — manageable with careful misting, but not engineered to the same no-haze standard as Techniseal's gel formula. At roughly $32-36 per 50-lb bag with coverage that stretches further than usual on a wide-joint job (because you're filling fewer total joints per square foot of patio), DOMINATOR #1 is the clear choice for flagstone, cobblestone, and any layout with joints wider than an inch.",
  },
  {
    id: "fortress-polymeric-sand",
    name: "Fortress Polymeric Sand",
    category: "Fine-Grain Polymeric Sand",
