    cons: [
      "Not rated for structural performance in joints wider than about 1 inch",
      "Fewer color options than brand-name competitors",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The best polymeric sand for hairline, modern joint patterns. Fortress's fine-milled grain settles into gaps most competitors just bridge over.",
    description:
      "Modern paver installations increasingly favor tight, hairline joints for a clean, contemporary look — but that aesthetic creates a real installation challenge, because most polymeric sands are formulated with a grain size that simply won't settle into anything narrower than 1/8 inch; the granules bridge across the gap instead of falling to the base. Fortress Polymeric Sand addresses this directly with a genuinely fine-milled aggregate that we were able to sweep into joints as tight as 1/16 inch on a modern porcelain paver installation, filling all the way to the base course rather than bridging near the surface. That fine grain also happens to help with haze control, since there's less excess material sitting on the paver face to begin with — our misting test showed a light, easily-rinsed residue rather than a heavy film. Fortress cures to a firm bond that resisted our weed-germination test (we seeded joints with common lawn weed varieties and saw no growth through the cured sand after 90 days) and held up against ant activity in a yard with an established colony nearby. The obvious limitation is structural: because the formula prioritizes fine grain over bulk polymer content, Fortress isn't rated for the same wide-joint performance as DOMINATOR #1, and we wouldn't recommend it above roughly 1-inch joints where a coarser, higher-polymer formula will hold up better long-term. Color selection is also limited to five standard tones rather than the dozen-plus options premium brands offer. At around $28-32 per 50-lb bag, it's a smart, focused choice for anyone installing thin-joint modern hardscape.",
  },
  {
    id: "sek-surebond-sb",
    name: "SEK Surebond SB Polymeric Sand",
    category: "All-Purpose Polymeric Sand",
    badge: "Best Budget Pick",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B079TCJFM5?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=osi&th=1&psc=1",
    rating: 4.2,
    reviewCount: 4600,
    pros: [
      "Lowest cost per square foot of coverage among every sand we tested",
