    id: "unilock-set-seal",
    name: "Unilock Set-Seal",
    category: "Color-Matched Polymeric Sand",
    badge: "Best Color Selection",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.6,
    reviewCount: 1800,
    pros: [
      "Broadest, most precisely calibrated color selection of any sand we tested, matched to popular paver aesthetic families",
      "Consistent color from bag to bag and batch to batch, avoiding the patchy look some sands develop across a large job",
      "Solid haze resistance and bond strength backed by a major paver manufacturer's material science team",
      "Performs reliably across the common 1/8 to 1.5 inch joint range",
      "Works well on any paver brand, not just Unilock products",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Priced at a premium alongside other top-tier sands, without a corresponding performance edge over Gator Maxx G2 or HP NextGel",
      "Primarily distributed through Unilock dealer networks, which can mean a longer drive or online order compared to big-box availability",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The pick for anyone who cares as much about a flawless, consistent finished color as raw technical performance.",
    description:
      "Color consistency is an underrated factor in a polymeric sand purchase — nothing undermines an otherwise excellent paver installation like joints that dry into two or three visibly different shades because of batch-to-batch color variation. Unilock, one of the largest paver manufacturers in North America, developed Set-Seal specifically to solve that problem for its own product lines, and the result is a sand with tighter color calibration than any generic competitor we tested. We laid out samples from three different bag lots side by side after full cure, and the color match across batches was effectively indistinguishable — something we couldn't say for two of the other sands in this roundup, which showed a noticeable shift between an older bag and a freshly opened one. Set-Seal's color library is built around the specific tones used in Unilock's paver and slab lines, but the sand itself is a generic, high-quality polymeric formula that bonds and performs well on any brand of paver, not just Unilock's own. Performance-wise, it lands solidly in the upper tier of this list — good haze resistance, a durable bond, and reliable coverage in the 1/8-to-1.5-inch joint range that covers most residential installations — without quite matching the extreme joint-width versatility of Gator Maxx G2 or the haze-elimination focus of HP NextGel. At roughly $36-40 per 50-lb bag and best sourced through Unilock dealer locations or their online store, it's the pick for anyone who cares as much about a flawless, consistent finished color as raw technical performance.",
